# PATCHES MUST STAY LF, ON EVERY PLATFORM.
#
# A .patch checked out with CRLF does not apply: git compares context lines byte for byte, the
# sources it patches are LF, and every hunk mismatches. On a Windows checkout with autocrlf that
# is exactly what happens to wasm-build/patches/osg-emscripten.patch — the whole wasm dependency
# stack is then unbuildable, and the error ("patch does not apply") points at the patch rather
# than at the checkout, which is the wrong place to go looking.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.diff text eol=lf

# Shell scripts likewise: a CRLF script fails with a bare `bad interpreter` or `\r: not found`,
# which says nothing useful about the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
